// 'o' has a hole, 'A' has a hole and a diagonal, 'i' is two separate
// contours, and 'e' acute is a composite -- so the four between them cover
// every branch in the outline reader that a Latin font can reach.
//
// The bounding box is what catches a sign or a delta error at once: a single
// wrong delta moves every point after it, and a wrong sign bit mirrors the
// glyph, and both show up in the box even though neither shows up in the
// point count.
tt_shapes() {
  int[] xs = [111, 65, 105, 233];
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len(xs)) {
    i = tt_shape1(xs, i);
  }
} return void;
given tt_fixture ():() then prints:("out 111 g 82 any 1 nc 2 np 24 bbox 113 -29 1141 1147 ends 11,23 on 100100100100100100100100\nout 65 g 36 any 1 nc 2 np 11 bbox 16 0 1384 1493 ends 2,10 on 11111111111\nout 105 g 76 any 1 nc 2 np 8 bbox 193 0 377 1556 ends 3,7 on 11111111\nout 233 g 171 any 1 nc 3 np 32 bbox 113 -29 1151 1638 ends 20,27,31 on 11100100110010010010010010011111\n")
